<title>BELGIUM: EU confirms four green rates to devalue on Sat.</title>
<headline>EU confirms four green rates to devalue on Sat.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Green rates for the Belgian franc, Dutch guilder, German mark and Austrian schilling will be devalued on Saturday, the European Commission confirmedy.</p>
<p>The green Belgian franc is to devalue to 40.4180 per Ecu from 40.3225, the German mark to 1.95903 per ecu from 1.95431, the Dutch guilder to 2.20270 per ecus from 2.19831 and the Austrian schilling to 13.7880 per Ecu from 13.7529, it said.</p>
<p>Green rates are used by the European Union to convert Ecus into the currencies of its member states in its Common Agricultural Policy.</p>
</text>
